{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu","id":1096800,"title":"Lunar: The Sidekick, the Silvermedal, the Pet Companion, the Waifu","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-25T11:39:22-07:00","id":1096800,"title":"Lunar: The Sidekick, the Silvermedal, the Pet Companion, the Waifu","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/uYTsJxj.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/EVdH1Br.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <hr /><br /> So Lunar's Charms being &quot;reskinned Solar Charms, but worse&quot; is going the way of the dodo in Ex3, but what about in the fluff though.<br /> <br /> I'm specifically curious about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> 1/ The relationships between the Solar and Lunar in the First Age ? How does the current Elder fell about it, what do they tell the younger Lunar about the Solar ?<br /> <br /> 2/ What would a (young) Lunar think when they see some Solar doing some of that &quot;Returned miracles&quot; stuffs i.e Solar circle spells, Ambition 3 Working, N/A artifacts ?<br /> <br /> 3/ Does &quot;A Lunar feel like they are the Vegata to Solar Goku&quot; a good character arc for Lunar ?<br /> <br /> 4/ If there is a Lunar and Solar PCs in your game, do you, or the player, feel the need to play up the metaphysical connection between the two characters ? How often are the Solar being the Lunar mate ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 06-19-2017, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T12:03:13-07:00","id":1096818,"title":"","content":"Ohhh you're playing with fire Jen, and I love it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu#post1096800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1/ The relationships between the Solar and Lunar in the First Age ? How does the current Elder fell about it, what do they tell the younger Lunar about the Solar ?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHmm, I have thoughts on this, but I feel as though they would mostly be rehashing (and maybe slightly elaborating) on what is already in the corebook, which might be a bit useless and maybe even a little bit condescending. I'll leave a pin in that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2/ What would a (young) Lunar think when they see some Solar doing some of that &quot;Returned miracles&quot; stuffs i.e Solar circle spells, Ambition 3 Working, N/A artifacts ?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHmm, that is interesting. After all, some of that is going to undeniably be the most impressive power in the setting, and the kind of thing that many have not seen in a long time. I'm sure that most will look on that with awe, but when it comes to at least Lunars who have been brought up with the stories of the Silver Pact, it might ring some alarm bells regarding the subject of their freedom from... everything in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">3/ Does &quot;A Lunar feel like they are the the Vegata to Solar Goku&quot; a good character arc for Lunar ?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou know, I could kind of see some of the general narrative beats in there. Obviously it's not exactly the same, but... if the Lunars have been without the Solars for a long time, then that would leave them as among the stronger individuals who have remained in the setting, and I could see somebody in there having quite an ego about it and getting very pissy about a Solar coming into their world and feeling like they're some Johnny-come-lately with more power than they deserve and being compelled by a desire to overcome and humble them.<br /> <br /> \u200bHmm, now I'm thinking of Vegeta in general... it's possible that I'm looking at it selectively, but I could actually see him as a source of inspiration for a character driven by a core of powerful Rage even as it expresses itself in nuanced and varied ways. I'll have to think about that...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T12:13:35-07:00","id":1096823,"title":"","content":"Those legs will haunt me in my nightmares....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T12:20:49-07:00","id":1096825,"title":"","content":"Imagine, for a moment, that Vegeta still had his tail and could transform whenever he wanted...<br /> <br /> As for the fluff, Holden went off on it long ago, in a post that I'm not sure we still have to reference. Then we got some landmark change notices when EX3 was announced, and a tweet from Holden about the time EX3 was finally released about bidding Edgelord Ma-Ha-Suchi bye forever. Hence, I doubt that we're going to be having to deal with the old albatrosses around the neck of the Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T13:01:01-07:00","id":1096834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu?p=1096825#post1096825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the fluff, Holden went off on it long ago</div> </div> </div> </div>The... Third Edition fluff?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence, I doubt that we're going to be having to deal with the old albatrosses around the neck of the Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but what about the things Jen asked about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T13:07:19-07:00","id":1096837,"title":"","content":"I cannot answer your question as I am spellbound by the implications of the Cerberus style Alex Jones in that second pic and what it would entail for the Exalted setting were I to implement it in a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12698-sunandspring","name":"SunAndSpring","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12698_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T14:05:29-07:00","id":1096860,"title":"","content":"I'm struggling for useful ways to respond to this. I think it's all more interesting if you look at the characters as individuals, and try not to think of them as trying to express a power relationship.<br /> <br /> For example, imagine a religious teacher inspired by a god like Luna, and who can experience life as a shapechanging variety of living forms. What might she believe and try to show people? Imagine one inspired by a god like the Unconquered Sun. Likewise. The power differences between the gods themselves and the chosen they empower should be the least interesting part of that interaction.<br /> <br /> I think it's the same thing about Solar miracles. What does the miracle do and why? That will inform how what the Lunar does is; react with awe, terror, rail against it, treat it as an amusing curiosity, exploit it to his advantage, try to defeat and overturn it, laugh at it as a powerful but fundamentally mistaken expression of hubris, and so on. I think that's the only way you'll be talking about an interesting response that isn't just rooted in these sort of stereotypical reactions that are quite boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T14:47:50-07:00","id":1096873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunAndSpring</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu?p=1096837#post1096837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Cerberus style Alex Jones in that second pic</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not Cerberus, that's the <i>literal</i> chimera. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's all more interesting if you look at the characters as individuals, and try not to think of them as trying to express a power relationship.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThere's always a bit of a balancing act isn't there? Sure there has to be individuality enough to be reasonably fleshed out characters, but some common trends are also likely, as well as useful for things like getting a handle on creating new characters and what might drive some stories.<br /> <br /> \u200bEven to say &quot;relationships between Lunars and their Solars were varied and complex&quot; is a commonality in itself, although there could conceivably be more beyond that.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't think Jen's question here is entirely a matter of looking at things in terms of characters being salty over tiers, although that might just be my bias. I'd say that there are a few things in setting in characterisation in which differences in type of strength between Solars and Lunars would be significant to relationships and conflicts, especially as it concerns things like what Lunars have been doing in the Second Age and what some common concerns about the returning Solars might be.<br /> ,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T22:25:49-07:00","id":1096983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu?p=1096818#post1096818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the stories of the Silver Pact</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, does it look like Ma-ha-suchi's rant in one of the Ex2 comic i.e generic &quot;Solar are hubris and arrogant but powerful =&gt; Dangerous&quot; or just straight up &quot;Solar are human possessed by demon !&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunAndSpring</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu?p=1096837#post1096837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot answer your question as I am spellbound by the implications of the Cerberus style Alex Jones in that second pic and what it would entail for the Exalted setting were I to implement it in a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;After meeting the Trinity of Delusional Truth, I started to see the hidden truth around me, the Dawn in my group......does his abs become ripper lately, and I can smell the sweat on his exploding muscle hiding beneath those black Gemenese leather.....Oh my glooobs, he's turning into a <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">HO</span><span style=\"color:#FF8C00\">MO</span><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">SE</span><span style=\"color:#008000\">XU</span><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">AA</span><span style=\"color:#EE82EE\">AL</span> !!!&quot;<br /> <br /> And yeah, it's actually a literal chimera like Isator said.....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu?p=1096860#post1096860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm struggling for useful ways to respond to this. I think it's all more interesting if you look at the characters as individuals, and try not to think of them as trying to express a power relationship.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Every characters are individuals and will have different reactions&quot; doesn't really grok my brain at all when it come to making plot hooks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm still new to this whole RPG and story-making thing so my lazy way is that I usually find a base/default reaction for each splat (DB Dynast want to kill Solar due to propaganda for example), create a character then see what they think about the default reaction, so a &quot;atheist&quot; Dynast who don't believe the Immaculate will probably more friendly to my Circle of Solar.<br /> <br /> As right now, I have no idea what kind of default reaction a Lunar will have when they see a Solar, and just saying &quot;every Lunar has different reaction&quot; just make all the enthusiastic flee my body........","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T22:51:38-07:00","id":1096986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu?p=1096983#post1096983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As right now, I have no idea what kind of default reaction a Lunar will have when they see a Solar, and just saying &quot;every Lunar has different reaction&quot; just make all the enthusiastic flee my body........</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking, Lunars have one of three attitudes when it comes to Solars.<br /> <br /> The first group is glad to the Solars come back. Maybe they think the Solars need run the world again. Maybe the don't want to see the Solars in charge, but they believe the Solars will make good allies against the Dragon Blooded. Maybe they don't even like Solars, but believe that whenever a Wyld Hunt kills a Solar, that means a Wyld Hunt <i>wasn't</i> killing a Lunar. In general, these guys view the Solar's return as a positive thing. These Lunars probably won't fight a Solar Exalted unless there's a good reason for it.<br /> <br /> The second group is unhappy about the Solars coming back. They've heard stories (or even remember) how crazy the Solars were during the First Age. They don't want the Solars in charge. They don't want things to go back to the First Age. They are quite happy with how things work now, and the Solars returning is only going to make everything worse. At best they view Solars as dangerous nuisances, at worst they view them as monsters. These Lunars may choose to try to kill a Solar when the opportunity presents itself. They ultimately consider the Solars to be a dangerous threat, either to their own plans, their existence or Creation itself.<br /> <br /> The last group of Lunars just don't care about the Solars. Maybe the Lunar is a scholar who spends much of her time in research. Maybe he lives out in the Wyld with the Fair Folk. Whatever the reason, the emergence of the Solar Exalted just doesn't concern this group of Lunars. How each one of this last group reacts to a Solar just depends - if the Solar is attacking the Fair Folk enclave where the Lunar is living as a guest, the Lunar might fight the Solar. If the Solar shows up and engages in diplomacy, the Lunar will probably respond in kind. For the scholar, if the Solar tries to attack and steal her knowledge, she would fight back. If the Solar asks her to teach him, she would just treat him like any other prospective student.<br /> <br /> For the most part, each Lunar is going to fall into one of these camps, and often their perception of the Solars is going to be formed by the stories they've heard about the Solars. Those who have studied under elder Exalted who have talked about how nightmarish the First Age was, and how tyrannical the Solars were, are probably going to be weary of the Solar Exalted. Those who studied under elder Lunars with more positive stories about the Solars will probably also be curious.<br /> <br /> Finally, don't forget that Lunars have past life memories. Lunars may suddenly have positive or negative memories and dreams about their previous incarnation's experiences with Solars, and those too might color the way a Lunar reacts when meeting a Solar. A Lunar who remembers the horrific torture he endured at the hands of his Solar mate will likely react rather differently than one who remembers the profound sense of love he felt for one of the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> *edit* Just to reiterate, I'm talking in broad generalities, not making absolute statements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-26-2017, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T23:25:46-07:00","id":1096999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu?p=1096986#post1096986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Generally speaking, Lunars have one of three attitudes when it comes to Solars.<br /> <br /> The first group is glad to the Solars come back. Maybe they think the Solars need run the world again. Maybe the don't want to see the Solars in charge, but they they believe the Solars will make good allies against the Dragon Blooded. Maybe they don't even like Solars, but believe that whenever a Wyld Hunt kills a Solar, that means a Wyld Hunt <i>wasn't</i> killing a Lunar. In general, these guys view the Solar's return as a positive thing. These guys probably won't fight a Solar Exalted unless there's a really good reason for it.<br /> <br /> The second group is unhappy about the Solars coming back. They've heard stories (or even remember) how crazy the Solars were during the First Age. They don't want the Solars in charge. They don't want things to go back to how they were. They view Solars as rivals who will try to create kingdoms, or even as very dangerous adversaries. These Lunars may choose to try to kill a Solar when the opportunity presents itself. They ultimately consider the Solars to be a dangerous threat, either to their own plans, their existence or Creation itself.<br /> <br /> The last group of Lunars just don't care about the Solars. Maybe the Lunar is a scholar who spends much of her time in research. Maybe he lives out in the Wyld with the Fair Folk. Whatever the reason, the emergence of the Solar Exalted just doesn't concern this group of Lunars. How each one of this last group reacts to a Solar just depends - if the Solar is attacking the Fair Folk enclave where the Lunar is living as a guest, the Lunar might fight the Solar. If the Solar shows up and engages in diplomacy, the Lunar will probably respond in kind. For the scholar, if the Solar tries to attack and steal her knowledge, she would fight back. If the Solar asks her to teach him, she would just treat him like any other prospective student.<br /> <br /> For the most part, each Lunar is going to fall into one of these camps, and often their perception of the Solars is going to be formed by the stories they've heard about the Solars. T<b>hose who have studied under elder Exalted who have talked about how nightmarish the First Age was, and how tyrannical the Solars were, are probably going to be weary of the Solar Exalted. Those who studied under elder Lunars with more positive stories about the Solars will probably also be curious.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that drum has been beaten more than enough for ten editions just from the way 2e handled it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, don't forget that Lunars have past life memories. Lunars may suddenly have positive or negative memories and dreams about their previous incarnation's experiences with Solars, and those too might color the way a Lunar reacts when meeting a Solar. A Lunar who remembers the horrific torture he endured at the hands of his Solar mate will likely react rather differently than one who remembers the profound sense of love he felt for one of the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> *edit* Just to reiterate, I'm talking in broad generalities, not making absolute statements. </div> </div> </div>I don't even think that you can really draw generalities. Lunars all have varying agendas, and how Solars get introduced in the drama of a situation can make a profound influence on how Lunars receive them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T23:25:56-07:00","id":1097000,"title":"","content":"a lunar is a dog that you get 3 bonus dice to roll to seduce through your ancient bond","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T23:27:00-07:00","id":1097001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu?p=1097000#post1097000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a lunar is a dog that you get 3 bonus dice to roll to seduce through your ancient bond</div> </div> </div> </div>We're discussing Lunars in third edition, not second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T00:02:29-07:00","id":1097013,"title":"","content":"Well the pact is probably going to emphasize that Solars are dangerous, that they can be useful and great but at the same that a good blade is still just as effective at stabbing you as stabbing someone else.On the other hand a solar has the capability to use the spell to specifically summon third circle demons come Calibration which really just destroy so many balances and situations. I mean come on Madelrada That Which Wears Down Mountains is apparently an extremely talented general and is able to potentially a wreck a siege situation by just staring at the enemy's walls until they dissolve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T00:59:32-07:00","id":1097030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu?p=1097001#post1097001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're discussing Lunars in third edition, not second.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we? We don't all seem to be.<br /> <br /> \u200bLike the idea of Lunars who don't care about Solars. That doesn't exactly seem to be possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu?p=1096983#post1096983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooh, does it look like Ma-ha-suchi's rant in one of the Ex2 comic i.e generic &quot;Solar are hubris and arrogant but powerful =&gt; Dangerous&quot; or just straight up &quot;Solar are human possessed by demon !&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bTo me, the corebook and several developer statements appear to be setting up a scenario in which the elder Lunars weave a narrative in which the Solars created something shining and beautiful that it was a real transgression for the Usurpers to dare to take away from the Lunar Exalted, at the same time as it was a highly compelling cage for them that they would be better off without.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, look at what it said in the core (he said to more than one person in the thread):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The return of the Solars changes everything for Luna\u2019s Chosen. Neither Lunar camp seeks to turn back the clock, nor wishes to return to defining themselves as the shadows cast by the Chosen of the sun. Something stirs in the Lunars\u2019 hearts, but none can yet say what it is or what it means. </div> </div> </div>\u200bIn a sense, it might not even be about the Solars, but about themselves, how they respond to Solars and how for many who have gone several lifetimes fighting to be free of the memory of the Realm, that's a response that they don't want anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T01:44:50-07:00","id":1097042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu?p=1096983#post1096983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still new to this whole RPG and story-making thing so my lazy way is that I usually find a base/default reaction for each splat (DB Dynast want to kill Solar due to propaganda for example), create a character then see what they think about the default reaction, so a &quot;atheist&quot; Dynast who don't believe the Immaculate will probably more friendly to my Circle of Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I understand. Well, though the reason you can talk about the default reaction for Dragonblooded or Sidereals is that they have big groups enforcing a similar view; the Immaculate religion, the Factions. That's why it kind of makes sense.<br /> <br /> For the Lunars in the books that's less pronounced, so it feels a bit harder to talk about a default view without getting into this idea of &quot;Oh, there's a stereotypical Lunar reaction that's not really based on the individual circumstances and characters at hand. Without any big social group really enforcing uniformity.&quot;. <br /> <br /> I think if you did want to make characters who have a default view, there's a bunch of different Lunar factions in the books (depending on your edition!), and then you can make a character's default view very strongly driven by his faction ideology (though that maybe probably tends to be pretty unlikely in the canon).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T02:05:18-07:00","id":1097046,"title":"","content":"Okay, one thing I always think is this:<br /> <br /> The Pact probably has no official line on Solars. They probably don't have a general training policy of telling Lunars to work with Solars, or fight them, or whatever.<br /> <br /> Because they've spent 1500 years living in a world with 400 Lunars and about 10 Solars. They're pretty irrelevant. The main purpose of Solars in Lunar historiography, is to prove how awful the Realm and its Sidereal masters are, for brutally massacring the Solars.<br /> Most Lunars never expected the Solars to return. They're used to a world without Solars.<br /> <br /> So, sure, now the Solars are coming back, their common attitudes are likely to be on a general level a)can we use them as a weapon against the Realm, b)are they going to try and rule us again, because screw that.<br /> <br /> But that's not going to be any kind of general policy, which is probably more a bunch of Elders arguing about what to do, and not having decided yet, because they're over 1000 years old and 5 years is nothing (not to mention that in the first year, it probably wasn't 100% clear what had happened).<br /> It's not like the Lunars have any easy way to force everyone to follow any kind of general policy.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also expect that the older Lunars are likely to have a lot more general view of the Solars (ie those guys who ran the Old Realm), while younger Lunars are more likely to view them much more individually (this Shining Spear of Victory girl is great, whipping up the natives against the Realm with her golden powers. Not like that Sun Magus in his tower always stealing magical texts. Those texts should be mine! I've been a sorcer for 100 years!).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T02:10:42-07:00","id":1097047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bTo me, the corebook and several developer statements appear to be setting up a scenario in which the elder Lunars weave a narrative in which the Solars created something shining and beautiful that it was a real transgression for the Usurpers to dare to take away from the Lunar Exalted, at the same time as it was a highly compelling cage for them that they would be better off without.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the impression I got as well.<br /> <br /> It could be argued that it's contradictory, but I think it's the sort of nuanced and complicated view that real people have of historical events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T02:20:52-07:00","id":1097053,"title":"","content":"Perhaps they'll be upset that Solar sorcerers tamper with the elemental essence of water and increase same-sex copulation in amphibians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T05:10:41-07:00","id":1097080,"title":"","content":"I'm not about to wade into a Lunar discussion, but I do want to say that Jen Art is Best Art and Also Most Horrifying Art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T07:33:02-07:00","id":1097118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu?p=1097047#post1097047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be argued that it's contradictory, but I think it's the sort of nuanced and complicated view that real people have of historical events.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh more than historical events, I think; all kinds of interpersonal interactions and standards of etiquette.<br /> <br /> \u200bLike taking insult over not having been extended an invitation to a party that you wouldn't have wanted to go to anyway.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt should also be remembered that the setup established in the core is that feeling a sense of loss for the Solars and the Realm is inherent to Lunars, that they all experience unpleasant dreams and visions of it. I find the significance of elders and storytellers of the Silver Pact to not be about providing answers, but context; not so much telling them the story of a lost world for which they would otherwise have no consideration as providing them with a frame of reference for vivid new sensations and impulses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T08:42:25-07:00","id":1097139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu?p=1096823#post1096823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those legs will haunt me in my nightmares....</div> </div> </div> </div>If tells are still a thing, I can only assume her totem animal thing is the emu or ostrich and absurdly long legs are her tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/723-talam","name":"Talam","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T14:10:35-07:00","id":1097288,"title":"","content":"I think Lunars will primarily see Solars through the lens of their respective personalities and the circumstances in which they meet, rather than judge by the color of a Caste mark.<br /> <br /> There will come a point sooner or later where the sheer power of Solars in some areas will provoke a reaction, but again the feeling will be about the person first, and the wielding of power second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T14:27:49-07:00","id":1097295,"title":"","content":"I think that's not entirely correct if they've heard the stories the Silver Pact will tell. The splat page for the Lunar Exalted on the core gives a strong impression that while the relationship is obviously flavored by the individual that Lunars collectively have a reaction of caution and potentially fear at the return of the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> But.. In fairness, that describes how basically <i>everyone</i> with any sort of knowledge reacts to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T15:46:55-07:00","id":1097334,"title":"","content":"I mean, I don't think it will be a case of &quot;gold anima bad&quot; so much as having a really weird sensation in which their soul simultaneously recoils in terror from this thing that they have a profound attraction to.<br /> <br /> Just imagine how confusing that must be. &quot;I don't know you! Except I really want you in my life! Except that being in my life would be an infringement on my freedom, so you fuck right off!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bTo be sure, I can imagine a diversity of ways in which people respond to this, but it seems to be the concept that they're going with; a complicated wash of emotions from vividly traumatic past life memories, the draw of the metaphysical connection intended for them from their ancient past, and the contemporary desire to achieve total freedom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T22:24:59-07:00","id":1097424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu?p=1097047#post1097047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the impression I got as well.<br /> <br /> It could be argued that it's contradictory, but I think it's the sort of nuanced and complicated view that real people have of historical events.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nuances such as the Lunar Exalted having realized that attaching yourself to someone who can disappear entirely can hurt like a sumbitch, and do you really want to risk them disappearing on you again? You still don't even know why they disappeared the first time, and don't know how or why they returned or whether it is permanent.<br /> <br /> Or nuances like, &quot;We could do without the Solars, but we're pissed that we didn't get to rule the Shogunate.&quot; Even if the world without Solars would have been lesser, it was still greater than the world left behind after the Dragon-Blooded wasted what was left on civil wars, and that's not counting the ruination of the Great Contagion or Fair Folk Invasion, which the Lunar Exalted might have been able to mitigate had they been in charge of a united Terrestrial Host with the assistance of the Sidereal Exalted and Bureau of Destiny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":