,"date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T12:27:40-07:00","id":1097586,"title":"","content":"What is that comic even meant to say in this context?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T12:56:20-07:00","id":1097598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu?p=1097586#post1097586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is that comic even meant to say in this context?</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, comparing how in 2E, when it came to respective Hero Styles and combat in general, Lunars often fell short of similarly experienced and specced Solars? Thus driving the Goku vs Vegeta comparison further?<br /> <br /> IDK.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T14:14:31-07:00","id":1097620,"title":"","content":"Makes sense. Sorry, saw that goddamn King Arthur movie earlier, and it's probably left me a bit touchy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T18:39:27-07:00","id":1097653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu?p=1097598#post1097598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um, comparing how in 2E, when it came to respective Hero Styles and combat in general, Lunars often fell short of similarly experienced and specced Solars? Thus driving the Goku vs Vegeta comparison further?<br /> <br /> IDK.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without cheap exploits like OaSB, anyway. 40 arms = 40 attacks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T10:40:59-07:00","id":1097821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu?p=1097295#post1097295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's not entirely correct if they've heard the stories the Silver Pact will tell. The splat page for the Lunar Exalted on the core gives a strong impression that while the relationship is obviously flavored by the individual that Lunars collectively have a reaction of caution and potentially fear at the return of the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> But.. In fairness, that describes how basically <i>everyone</i> with any sort of knowledge reacts to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm bringing my personal biases in, but to me all this &quot;How will the Lunars react!?&quot; talk reminds me a lot of the problems of 2E with a new coat of paint. In 2E, of course, people recoiled from things like the Bond and the Silver Solar charms. I can see a few years from now people finding the Love-Hate-Fear dynamic a little tiresome, too. When do these great heroes move past their little serial numbers and start acting like characters?<br /> <br /> So, I'm importing a small bit of V:tM thinking to keep the setting fresh. &quot;Exalts are people first, heroes second, and Chosen of their patron last.&quot;<br /> <br /> I am not looking forward to RP'ing this fairly narrow path of interaction with every single Lunar my Solar PC might meet, and I'll be damned if I run every Lunar-Solar meeting that way when I'm ST'ing. How boring for my players, regardless of their splat. I can already hear my future players saying &quot;Oh, does <b>this </b>Lunar hate me, worship me, fear me, or all three?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T13:59:20-07:00","id":1097868,"title":"","content":"I don't really think it's an obligation to type besides how more elemental feelings might inform them, but I guess my point was more that everybody reacts with caution when any potentially powerful group of people is suddenly involved in things.<br /> <br /> But I admit I also don't see at all how this is mutually exclusive with being people first, because this is what people do. They're informed of information that might color their perspective and integrate that information in different ways. I think the point of the talk of caution is just to ensure that people don't assume that Solars and Lunars are all going to immediately align with one another because they are both hated and feared by the Realm as anathema. In fact they are more complicated in terms of the baggage they bring to a relationship than simply being friendly, which ideally is true of every relationship between complicated, powerful people. It's just about providing enough context for why the Silver Pact isn't rocking gold chains just yet.<br /> <br /> I think the way fans parse this kind of information can be a bit reactionary but the book takes a more appropriately measured tone for expressing the ambivalence, and I would stick with that as a guide for developing ideas around this sort of stuff. The point isn't that Lunars are obligated to hate or love them, just a narrative reminder that their feelings are probably more complicated about the guys they've heard these stories about than just simply thinking that the enemy of my enemy is my friend. Which is good! More drama, more plot hooks. That's great. Reminds people of the options they have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 05-28-2017, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T19:34:40-07:00","id":1097938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu?p=1097573#post1097573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did plan to go for a normal Lunar pic at first, but when I heard that there is some kind of Changing Moon faction who likes conspiracy theories all I can think about is Alex Jones as a Lunar.......</div> </div> </div> </div>Not technically a Changing Moon faction as such, as everyone in it was Casteless or wanted to be, if you even have it as a thing that existed in your campaigns (it's paracanon on the order of Nox and the Nocturnal Exalted). It's another bit of 2e-ism where a group of Lunars whines about their own kind like they whine about the Solars, in this case, claiming that the Changing Moon caste is a slap in the face to the Changing Moon Society, because the No Moons co-opted their name and ugh won't EX3 just make the hurting stop already and wipe this away?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T10:24:31-07:00","id":1098138,"title":"","content":"Madame Vert and her society actually considered ALL Lunar Castes to be a scam and the Silver Pact to be con-artists. These Casteless Lunars believed that Luna wanted them to be Casteless from the beginning and that only in Castelessness could they enjoy true Lunar power.<br /> <br /> <br /> And yeah, I really wish I could throw myself completely into being hyped for the new and improved Dragon-Blooded or anything else 3rd Edition is doing, but there's always a voice in my heart that says, &quot;But what about the Luuuuuunars?&quot; and it steals some of my joy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}